-- Work-email check, which row it was made on (Testing Run 5, T95): job_email_checks.role_source, "resume" or "added", the side of the profile the checked job was on when the check passed, so a resume role and a role added on Me that share company and start month never both take the badge. Nullable with no default: checks saved before this keep null and fall back to the old rule (the company as written, then the current row). On job_email_checks, which has row level security on already; no foreign key, so no new index. Expand only: one nullable column and its check; old code never writes it.
ALTER TABLE "job_email_checks" ADD COLUMN "role_source" text;--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "job_email_checks" ADD CONSTRAINT "job_email_checks_role_source" CHECK ("job_email_checks"."role_source" is null or "job_email_checks"."role_source" in ('resume', 'added'));
